  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an undirected graph GGG with NNN nodes, where every node is initially uncolored, Chef colors its vertices either red or blue by the following process:\n\n\nChef will perform exactly NNN coloring operations, one for each vertex.\nAt the time of the iii-th operation, let RRR denote the number of red nodes and BBB denote the number of blue nodes.\n\nChef colors node iii red with a probability of R+1R+B+2\\frac{R+1}{R+B+2}R+B+2R+1​, or blue with a probability of B+1R+B+2\\frac{B+1}{R+B+2}R+B+2B+1​\nNote that vertices must be colored in the order 1,2,3,…,N1, 2, 3, \\ldots, N1,2,3,…,N.\n\nFor this graph GGG, f(G)f(G)f(G) is defined to be the probability that the resulting coloring is proper — that is, no two adjacent vertices should share the same color.\n\nChef starts off with an empty graph with NNN nodes and no edges. He then adds MMM undirected edges to the graph in the order (u1,v1),(u2,v2),…,(uM,vM)(u_1,v_1),(u_2,v_2), \\ldots ,(u_M,v_M)(u1​,v1​),(u2​,v2​),…,(uM​,vM​).\n\nOutput the value of f(G)f(G)f(G) after each edge has been added to the graph, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n**Note:** It can be shown that the required probability can be represented as a fraction PQ\\frac{P}{Q}QP​ where PPP and QQQ are non-negative integers such that gcd⁡(P,Q)=1\\gcd(P, Q) = 1gcd(P,Q)=1 and 998244353998244353998244353 doesn't divide QQQ.\n\nThere will be a unique integer RRR such that 0≤R&lt;9982443530 \\leq R \\lt 9982443530≤R&lt;998244353 and P≡Q⋅R(mod998244353)P \\equiv Q\\cdot R \\pmod{998244353}P≡Q⋅R(mod998244353). Print this integer RRR.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM — the number of vertices and edges of the graph, respectively.\nThe next MMM lines describe the edges. The iii-th of these MMM lines contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nAfter each edge addition, output the value of f(G)f(G)f(G), modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "2≤N≤50002 \\leq N \\leq 50002≤N≤5000",
      "1≤M≤min⁡(N(N−1)2,&nbsp;2⋅105)1 \\leq M \\leq \\min(\\frac{N(N-1)}{2},\\space2\\cdot10^5)1≤M≤min(2N(N−1)​,&nbsp;2⋅105)",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "ui≠viu_i \\neq v_iui​=vi​ for each 1≤i≤M1 \\leq i \\leq M1≤i≤M",
      "Each unordered pair (ui,vi)(u_i,v_i)(ui​,vi​) occurs at most once.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 500050005000.",
      "The sum of MMM over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot10^52⋅105."
    ],
